    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "FLY\nTO MEXICO • WEST INDIES\nCENTRAL and SOUTH AMERICA\nHAVANA • MEXICO\nCITY • NASSAU\nLindbergh,\nGUATEMALA\nSAN SALVADOR\nMANAGUA\nCRISTOBAL\nPANAMA CITY\nTURBO\nCARTAGENA\nPUNTARENAS\nDAVID\nFLIGHT SCHEDULE\nMARACAY\nPAN AMERICAN AIRWAYS SYSTEM\nPORT e\"\nSPAIN",
      "PAAR\n§ Lindberghs\nCircle\nRoute\nPan American Airways\noffer de luxe Air Passenger service, saving days\nand weeks of travel time, on 3,500 miles of model\nMexico, Cuba,\nHaiti,\nairways to Nassal, Porto Rico, Republic of\nDominican\nRepublic,\nPanama, Panama Canal Zone and (by Pan Ameri-\ncan Grace Airways) Ecuador and Peru.\nAn additional 4,000 miles of airways, serving\nHonduras, British Honduras,\nNicaragua, Costa\nRica, Colombia and Curacao are also operated on\nregular schedues tor air mail under United States\nPost Office Department contracts. Passenger ser-\nvice over these routes will be inaugurated as rapid-\nly as every detail for the comfort and safety of\npassengers is completed.\nPan American Airways operate only three-engined,\n12 passenger de luxe transports or twin-engined, 8\npassenger amphibions on all passenger routes. All\nPan American airliners, comprising the largest fleet\nof multi-motor aircraft in the world. are com-\npletely radio-equipped and carry licensed radio\noperators.\nInformation, reservations and through tickets are\navailable at principal railway ticket offices and\nselect travel bureaus throughout the United States.\nPan American Airways, Ic.\nExecutive Offices—122 E. 42d Street\nNew York City\nand all points on the airways"
    ],
